        $note .= '<h5>Procedures used to establish the assigned value:</h5>';
        $note .= '<span style="text-align:justify;font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;">The results of participating laboratories using the same VL platform were grouped together and analyzed for peer-comparison using the normalized InterQuartile Range (nIQR) method. The nIQR method uses the median as the assigned value because it is a robust estimator of central tendency that is less influenced by outliers. This approach ensures that the assigned value remains representative of the central distribution of participant results, even when a proportion of results may be extreme or atypical. Assigned value, Robust Standard Deviation, Standard Uncertainty of assigned value, z score and performance score were derived as per the Standard ISO13528: 2022(E). A VL platform with the most participants was used as a reference value to evaluate results for VL platforms with less than eighteen participants in this PT round.</span>';

        $pdf->writeHTML($note, true, false, true, false, '');

        // Criteria and interval are indented with the formulas set apart in bold, as in the summary template
        $note = '<table cellpadding="2" style="width:100%;"><tr><td style="width:7%;"></td><td style="width:93%;font-size:12px;">';
        $note .= '<br/><strong>Acceptable Performance Criteria</strong><br/>';
        $note .= '<span style="text-align:justify;">Acceptable performance is defined as achieving a z-score with an absolute value less than 3.0 (|z| &lt; 3.0), where the z-score is calculated as:</span><br/>';
        $note .= '<strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;z = (Participant Result &ndash; Assigned Value) / Robust SD</strong><br/>';
        $note .= '<strong>Acceptable Result Interval</strong><br/>';
        $note .= 'For each sample, an Acceptable Result Interval is calculated and reported as:<br/>';
        $note .= '<strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Assigned Value &plusmn; (3 &times; Robust SD)</strong><br/>';
        $note .= 'Results falling within this interval are considered acceptable performance (|z| &lt; 3.0).';
        $note .= '</td></tr></table>';
        $pdf->writeHTML($note, true, false, true, false, '');

        $note = '<span style="text-align:justify;font-size:12px;color:#0A2F41;"><strong>(Robust Standard Deviation (SD)</strong> in the nIQR method is a dispersion estimate calculated as 0.7413 &times; (Q3 &minus; Q1), where Q1 and Q3 are the 25th and 75th percentiles of participant results. It provides a resistant estimate of variability that is less influenced by outliers than the classical standard deviation.)</span><br/>';

        /* $note .= '<h5>Subcontracting:</h5>';
        $note .= '<span style="text-align:justify;font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;">Only the transport of PT items and the ePT site administration are subcontracted.</span>'; */
        $note .= '<h5>Cooperative Agreement (CoAg) Partner:</h5>';
        $note .= '<span style="text-align:justify;font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;">Only the transport of PT items and the ePT site administration are managed by a CoAg.</span>';

        $note .= '<h5>Confidentiality:</h5>';
        $note .= '<span style="text-align:justify;font-size:11px;font-weight:normal;">The identities of participants are kept confidential and known only to the staff involved in the implementation of the Proficiency Testing.  Each participant has been assigned a unique identification number for the purposes of database management.</span>';

        $pdf->writeHTML($note, true, false, true, false, '');

        if (isset($resultArray['shipment']['shipment_comment']) && $resultArray['shipment']['shipment_comment'] != "") {

            $html = '<table border="1" cellpadding="3">
                        <tr>
                            <td style="text-align:left;font-size:11px;font-weight:bold;">' . $resultArray['shipment']['shipment_comment'] . '</td>
